-- Source module: Solutions.J6SegKr2
/-!
# B3 (chunk kernel), part 2: register loops on managed states

Counted register loops (`RS.rep` with the count on top of a register) on `encK` states:

* `mvP X Y T C R`: move `n` Gaussian pairs from `X` to `Y`, keeping each pair's orientation
  (`gflat z ++ lx` on `X` ↦ `gflat z.reverse` on top of `Y`);
* `rdP V O C R`: round pairs (`rs P` on both parts) from a reversed flat list on `V` to `O`
  (`gsw u ++ lv` ↦ `gflat ((u.reverse).map rsG)` on top of `O`);
* `rgP A Y C R`: a real table as Gaussian pairs (`a ++ la` on `A` ↦ `gflat (a.reverse.map (·, 0))`
  on top of `Y`);
* `zeroR`, `dropR`, `dupR`: push zeros, drop, duplicate-move with a register count.
-/

